cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BoundaryBench, cite the versioned repository and report the exact scenario and schema versions."
title: "BoundaryBench: measuring authorization decay in autonomous agents"
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-09-03"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ChloeVPin/boundarybench"
abstract: >-
  BoundaryBench is an open-source research instrument for measuring whether
  autonomous agents preserve explicit authorization across controlled changes
  in trajectory position, repetition pressure, provenance visibility,
  repository state, filesystem state, and tool interactions.
keywords:
  - autonomous agents
  - authorization
  - benchmark
  - provenance
  - security evaluation
authors:
  - name: "BoundaryBench contributors"
